# <%= name %>

<%= tool[:description] %>

This gem packages the `<%= tool[:executable] %>` command of [`@herb-tools/<%= tool[:package] %>`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@herb-tools/<%= tool[:package] %>) as a standalone executable, so it can be used without Node.js.

```bash
bundle add <%= name %> --group development
bundle exec <%= tool[:executable] %> --help
```

The `herb` gem's `herb <%= tool[:executable].delete_prefix("herb-") %>` command uses this executable when the gem is installed.

On platforms without a standalone executable, like 32-bit ARM and x86 Linux, it runs the npm package with `npx` instead when Node.js is available.

See the [documentation](https://herb-tools.dev) for more details.
